message.content:
This is a check valve of plastic (polypropylene composite) used in a vehicle cooling circuit. It is classified in heading 8481, valves for pipes, tanks, and the like. The check (non-return) valve subheading is 8481.30. Within it, 8481.30.10 covers those of iron or steel, 8481.30.20 covers those of copper, and 8481.30.90 covers other. In CBP rulings, plastic check valves fall under 8481.30.9090 ("Other"). The 8481.30.90 split is: 8481.30.9010 is of plastics? I'm not certain. I recall 8481.80.50 for plastic valves, but that is for other appliances. For check valves, 8481.30.20 is "Of copper", and 8481.30.90 is "Other", which I believe has the statistical suffixes 8481.30.9040 and 8481.30.9060. Because I can't verify them, I'll go with 8481.30.9090.

Section XVII parts are excluded by Note 2 to Section XVII, since heading 8481 goods are not parts of vehicles under that section. Heading 8481 therefore applies.

{"hts_code": "8481.30.9090", "reason": "A plastic spring-loaded check (non-return) valve is classified in heading 8481 as a check valve, in the 'other' subheading 8481.30.90, and is excluded from Section XVII vehicle parts by Section XVII Note 2(f)."}
